{"content":[{"c":["KAIN* (Tribe)"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Clan name synonymous with the Kenites (",{"href":"?bref=Num.24.22","r":"Num.24.22","rawR":"Num.24.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.24.22","value":"Num.24.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 24:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.4.11","r":"Judg.4.11","rawR":"Judg.4.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.4.11","value":"Judg.4.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 4:11"},"). The name is Hebrew for “spear,” suggesting a tribe of metalworkers. The nomadic tribe was friendly (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.15.6","r":"1Sam.15.6","rawR":"1Sam.15.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.15.6","value":"1Sam.15.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 15:6"},") and was eventually absorbed by Judah. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Kenites_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Kenites_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Kenites_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Kenites"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"KainTribe","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 24:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.24.22","rawQueryValue":"Num.24.22","sourceRefExact":"Num.24.22"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 4:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.4.11","rawQueryValue":"Judg.4.11","sourceRefExact":"Judg.4.11"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 15:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.15.6","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.15.6","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.15.6"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"8897cf5e7a2d7c430a4aa880ef6f767b5a562d81bec01e43ec0816ca5311e44a","sourceItemName":"KainTribe","sourceItemOrder":7,"sourceMember":"Articles/K.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"KainTribe","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Art